                      (   unit_tests.asm):00426                                             ; the interrupt-driven EMIT (SERIALPOLL=0). Real
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00427                                             ; bug found via MAME: EMIT has two entirely
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00428                                             ; different implementations, gated the same way
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00429                                             ; as KEY's own two variants - the polling one
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00430                                             ; (SERIALPOLL=1, confirmed the currently active
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00431                                             ; build) writes directly to ACIADR and never
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00432                                             ; touches OUTHEAD/OUTBUF at all, so that check
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00433                                             ; always failed despite the character genuinely
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00434                                             ; being transmitted (confirmed in the terminal
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00435                                             ; output itself). EMITCH, by contrast, is set
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00436                                             ; unconditionally by both variants as their very
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00437                                             ; first step, before either mode-specific branch
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00438                                             ; - checking it verifies the argument was
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00439                                             ; correctly extracted from the stack regardless
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00440                                             ; of which EMIT variant is active, with no
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00441                                             ; conditional needed.
