                      (   unit_tests.asm):03386         ; TSTDARITH - mixed & double-precision arithmetic tests (glossary
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03387         ; section 3.5). Covers every word in that section. All 14 words
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03388         ; traced by hand against their real implementations before any
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03389         ; test was written - push/pop order for double-cell values (low
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03390         ; cell pushed first, high cell last/on top - confirmed identical
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03391         ; across every word here), and which of two operands is which
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03392         ; (d1 vs d2, dividend vs divisor) - not assumed from the glossary
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03393         ; stack-effect notation alone. FM/MOD (floored) and SM/REM
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03394         ; (symmetric) tested against the same negative-dividend case
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03395         ; specifically because that's where the two conventions actually
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03396         ; diverge - confirmed distinct expected results for each.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03397         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03398         ; TSTUMSM2 (added later) is a dedicated boundary-case regression
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03399         ; test for UM/MOD's own ANS Annex F MAX-UINT/MAX-UINT case
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03400         ; (F.6.1.2370), on top of TSTUMSM's ordinary mid-range case - see
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03401         ; TSTUMSM2's own header/comment for why only UM/MOD, of every word
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03402         ; in this section, can actually reach the UDIV32 bug it regression-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03403         ; tests (the other division words here all derive UDIV32's divisor
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03404         ; from a signed single cell, too narrow a range to trigger it).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03405         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
