                      (   unit_tests.asm):07332         ; TSTDEFWORDS - defining-words tests (glossary section 3.9, 17
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07333         ; words, 12 tests since VALUE/TO and IS/ACTION-OF are each
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07334         ; combined into one test). Every defining word parses a name
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07335         ; from the input source via WORD (HEADER's own mechanism,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07336         ; shared by :/CREATE) - a complexity nothing in section 3.8 had.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07337         ; Each test redirects CODEHERE, DPHERE, VARHERE, and
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07338         ; SRCADDR/SRCLEN/TOIN together (a fake name, "TESTWD", reused
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07339         ; safely across every test here since each redirect/restore
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07340         ; cycle is fully isolated), calls the real defining word
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07341         ; directly, saves the newly-defined word's own CFA (= CODEHERE
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07342         ; at the moment the defining word was called), restores
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07343         ; everything, then executes that CFA directly to verify runtime
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07344         ; behavior.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07345         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07346         ; A real, structurally important finding from this section:
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07347         ; HEADER writes to the real LATEST variable unconditionally, not
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07348         ; a redirectable copy like CODEHERE/DPHERE/VARHERE - every test
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07349         ; here explicitly saves and restores it, confirmed necessary by
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07350         ; reading HEADER's own code directly, not assumed safe by analogy
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07351         ; with the other three pointers.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07352         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07353         ; MARKER's own test is the one exception to the general
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07354         ; redirect-then-restore-then-execute order: DOMARKER (confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07355         ; by reading it directly) writes to the real DPHERE/CODEHERE/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07356         ; VARHERE/LATEST unconditionally too, so that test executes the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07357         ; marker word while still redirected, only restoring the real
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07358         ; environment afterward - getting this order backwards would
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07359         ; have corrupted the real dictionary pointers with scratch
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07360         ; addresses.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07361         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07362         ; Bare CREATE (never followed by DOES>) is deliberately not
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07363         ; tested on its own - traced its placeholder "behavior field"
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07364         ; (a genuine compiled JSR DOESRT0 instruction) and confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07365         ; DODOES reads that field as raw data, not as code to execute -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07366         ; which only produces a valid jump target for the raw-address
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07367         ; form every other defining word uses (VARIABLE, CONSTANT, etc,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07368         ; via CODECOMMA), not CREATE's own placeholder JSR instruction.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07369         ; Bare CREATE's own direct-execution behavior isn't meant to be
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07370         ; relied upon before a DOES> patches it.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07371         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
