                      (   unit_tests.asm):07405         ; Defining-words test harness (glossary section 3.9). Every
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07406         ; defining word parses a name from the input source via WORD -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07407         ; unlike anything in section 3.8's control-flow tests - so each
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07408         ; test redirects CODEHERE, DPHERE, VARHERE, and SRCADDR/SRCLEN/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07409         ; TOIN together (a fake name text, "TESTWD", reused safely
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07410         ; across every test here since each redirect/restore cycle is
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07411         ; fully isolated), calls the real defining word directly, saves
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07412         ; the newly-defined word's own CFA (= CODEHERE at the moment the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07413         ; defining word was called), restores everything, then executes
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07414         ; that CFA directly to verify runtime behavior. Traced by hand:
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07415         ; CREATE/VARIABLE/CONSTANT/etc all use HEADER (shared header-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07416         ; building) then compile a fixed 5-byte trampoline (3-byte
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07417         ; "JSR DODOES" + a 2-byte "behavior field") before their own
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07418         ; PFA - confirmed the behavior field holds a genuine compiled
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07419         ; JSR instruction only for CREATE's own bare placeholder
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07420         ; (DOESRT0, later patched by DOES>); every other defining word
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07421         ; (VARIABLE, CONSTANT, DEFER, MARKER, VALUE) instead compiles a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07422         ; raw 2-byte address there directly (via CODECOMMA, not CCALL) -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07423         ; DODOES reads this field as data either way, which only works
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07424         ; correctly for the raw-address form. This is why bare CREATE,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07425         ; executed before any DOES>, isn't tested here - its own
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07426         ; placeholder behavior field isn't meant to be read as data,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07427         ; only ever overwritten by DOES> before first use.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07428         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07429         
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07430         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
