                      (   unit_tests.asm):08698         ; "TESTWD" via WORD+FIND, needing LATEST still pointed at it -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08699         ; not restored until this whole test finishes), executes TESTWD
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08700         ; (should now behave like DUP), then interprets "ACTION-OF
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08701         ; TESTWD" to fetch the current target by name and confirms it
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08702         ; matches DUP's own xt. Explicitly forces STATE=0 before both IS
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08703         ; and ACTION-OF, since both are documented to behave differently
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08704         ; by STATE, same reasoning as TSTVALTO's own TO test.
