                      (   unit_tests.asm):13594         ; TSTNUMOUT - numeric output tests (glossary section 3.13, 14
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13595         ; words, 13 tests since #S and #> are combined into one test,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13596         ; matching how they're naturally used together as the tail of
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13597         ; the standard pictured-output idiom "<# ... #S #>").
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13598         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13599         ; The pictured-numeric-output core (<# # #S #> HOLD HOLDS) is
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13600         ; pure string-building with no I/O, tested directly. SIGN
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13601         ; carries real bug-fix history - a prior bare BPL right after
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13602         ; PULU didn't affect condition codes on real 6809 hardware, and
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13603         ; the bug was masked for every internal caller by caller-side
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13604         ; luck (each ran a flag-setting LDD right before calling SIGN).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13605         ; This section's own SIGN test deliberately poisons the flags
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13606         ; with an unrelated CMPX immediately before each direct call,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13607         ; so it exercises the exact previously-broken scenario rather
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13608         ; than repeating the same kind of luck that hid the bug.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13609         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13610         ; The high-level printing words (./U./.R/U.R/?/D./D.R) all
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13611         ; produce real output via TYPE/EMIT internally, so each applies
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13612         ; the SERIALPOLL-conditional split established in section 3.1 -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13613         ; full OUTHEAD/OUTBUF verification under SERIALPOLL=0, an
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13614         ; EMITCH-based last-character check under SERIALPOLL=1. .R/U.R/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13615         ; D.R specifically test the padding path (a width wider than the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13616         ; actual digits), not just a no-padding sanity case. D./D.R use
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13617         ; a genuine double-cell value (-100000, computed and verified
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13618         ; independently in Python before writing the tests) to exercise
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13619         ; the 32-bit negation path, not a value that happens to fit in
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13620         ; one cell.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13621         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13622         ; Note: this section's own COMPARE-adjacent naming risk doesn't
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13623         ; apply here, but every group wrapper name (TSTNUMOUT) and every
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13624         ; internal FAIL/DONE prefix was still checked against the whole
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13625         ; file before insertion, per the standard practice that caught
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13626         ; the TSTCOMPARE collision in the prior section.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13627         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
