                      (   unit_tests.asm):13662         ; Numeric Output test harness (glossary section 3.13). The
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13663         ; pictured-numeric-output core (<# # #S #> HOLD HOLDS SIGN) is
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13664         ; pure string-building with no I/O, tested directly. The
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13665         ; high-level printing words (./U./.R/U.R/?/D./D.R) all produce
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13666         ; real output via TYPE and/or EMIT internally, so per section
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13667         ; 3.1's own already-debugged finding, each applies the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13668         ; SERIALPOLL-conditional split established there: full OUTHEAD/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13669         ; OUTBUF verification under SERIALPOLL=0, an EMITCH-based check
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13670         ; of the last character under SERIALPOLL=1 - accepted as a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13671         ; known, honest limitation for words ending in a trailing space
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13672         ; (./U./D. all print a fixed final space character, so the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13673         ; polling-mode check there confirms less than for the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13674         ; no-trailing-space words, but is still correct and consistent
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13675         ; with the same trade-off already established for TSTCR/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13676         ; TSTSPACES/TSTTYPE/TSTDOTQUOTE in earlier sections).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13677         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13678         ; SIGN itself carries real bug-fix history: a prior version used
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13679         ; a bare BPL immediately after PULU, which doesn't affect
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13680         ; condition codes on real 6809 hardware - the bug was masked for
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13681         ; every internal caller by "caller-side luck" (each happened to
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13682         ; run a flag-setting LDD right before calling SIGN). This
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13683         ; section's own SIGN test deliberately poisons the flags with an
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13684         ; unrelated, known-positive value immediately before the actual
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13685         ; PSHU/JSR SIGN sequence specifically so a standalone call - the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13686         ; exact scenario the bug-fix comment says was previously broken
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13687         ; - is what gets tested, not a scenario that happens to work via
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13688         ; the same kind of caller-side luck that hid the original bug.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13689         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13690         
