                      (   unit_tests.asm):15488         ; TSTENVSYS - environmental & system queries tests (glossary
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15489         ; section 3.17, 10 words, 8 tests since TIB/#TIB/>IN/SPAN/BL are
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15490         ; combined into one test, and ENVIRONMENT? gets three separate
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15491         ; tests of its own - single-cell, double-cell, and unsupported-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15492         ; string cases).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15493         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15494         ; REFILL genuinely blocks on real input when the source is the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15495         ; terminal (confirmed by reading its own code: the terminal
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15496         ; branch calls QUERY, which per section 3.1's own already-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15497         ; established finding calls ACCEPT, which calls KEY, which spins
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15498         ; forever without real input) - only its safely-testable path
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15499         ; (source is a string) is tested here, matching the same
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15500         ; reasoning already applied to KEY/ACCEPT/EXPECT/QUERY
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15501         ; themselves. EVALUATE genuinely executes its given string as
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15502         ; real Forth source via JSR INTERPRET - confirmed safe via
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15503         ; INTERPRET's own code (it simply stops when input is exhausted,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15504         ; no automatic REFILL, so no blocking risk), making a short,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15505         ; deliberately harmless string ("1 2 +") safe to evaluate
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15506         ; directly.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15507         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15508         ; ENVIRONMENT? carries substantial, already-documented bug-fix
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15509         ; history (a COMPAREW-clobbers-X bug, confirmed via MAME with the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15510         ; exact $4E4D symptom). This section's own tests specifically
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15511         ; query "/COUNTED-STRING" immediately followed by "MAX-N" - the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15512         ; exact adjacent pair the bug-fix comment describes - so a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15513         ; regression of that specific mechanism would be caught again,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15514         ; not just assumed fixed from the comment alone.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15515         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
