                      (   unit_tests.asm):15545         ; Environmental & System Queries test harness (glossary section
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15546         ; 3.17). Five words (TIB/#TIB/>IN/SPAN/BL) are simple constant/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15547         ; variable readers, combined into one test rather than five
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15548         ; separate ones, matching the established approach from section
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15549         ; 3.14's own TSTBASE.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15550         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15551         ; REFILL genuinely blocks on real input when the source is the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15552         ; terminal (confirmed by reading its own code directly: the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15553         ; terminal branch calls QUERY, which - per section 3.1's own
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15554         ; already-established finding - calls ACCEPT, which calls KEY,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15555         ; which spins forever without real input). Only its safely-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15556         ; testable path (source is a string, SRCID<>0) is tested here,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15557         ; matching the same reasoning already applied to KEY/ACCEPT/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15558         ; EXPECT/QUERY themselves in section 3.1.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15559         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15560         ; EVALUATE genuinely executes its given string as real Forth
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15561         ; source via JSR INTERPRET - confirmed via INTERPRET's own code
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15562         ; that it simply stops and returns when input is exhausted (no
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15563         ; automatic REFILL, so no blocking risk), making a short,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15564         ; deliberately harmless string ("1 2 +") safe to evaluate
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15565         ; directly.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15566         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15567         ; ENVIRONMENT? carries substantial, already-documented bug-fix
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15568         ; history (a COMPAREW-clobbers-X bug, confirmed via MAME with the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15569         ; exact $4E4D symptom - reading two bytes of the NEXT table
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15570         ; entry's own name text as if they were the current entry's
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15571         ; value). This section's own tests specifically query
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15572         ; "/COUNTED-STRING" immediately followed by "MAX-N" - the exact
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15573         ; adjacent pair the bug-fix comment describes - so a regression
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15574         ; of that specific mechanism would be caught again, not just
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15575         ; assumed fixed from the comment alone.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15576         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15577         
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15578         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
