                      (   unit_tests.asm):15860                     LDD   #TSTCBUF2         ; SECOND BUG FIX: the LATEST fix above
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15861                     STD   CODEHERE          ; alone didn't resolve this - confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15862                                             ; via a second MAME run (the failure
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15863                                             ; persisted, with the terminal output
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15864                                             ; varying between runs, a strong sign
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15865                                             ; of memory corruption rather than a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15866                                             ; single deterministic missing-value
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15867                                             ; problem). Root cause: CODEHERE, like
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15868                                             ; BASE and LATEST, is only set by COLD
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15869                                             ; and was never redirected by this
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15870                                             ; test at all - unlike every other
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15871                                             ; test in this whole session involving
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15872                                             ; WORD (which EVALUATE's own internal
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15873                                             ; JSR INTERPRET calls repeatedly, once
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15874                                             ; per token). With CODEHERE=0
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15875                                             ; (unredirected), WORD's own write of
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15876                                             ; each parsed token's [len][text]
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15877                                             ; landed straight at address $0000 -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15878                                             ; which is STATE's own address (offset
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15879                                             ; $00, the very first bytes of
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15880                                             ; GLOBALS, confirmed by re-reading its
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15881                                             ; own RMB declaration directly). Even
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15882                                             ; a single-character token like "1"
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15883                                             ; overwrites STATE with a nonzero
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15884                                             ; value, flipping INTERPRET into
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15885                                             ; thinking it's compiling rather than
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15886                                             ; interpreting mid-parse - explaining
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15887                                             ; both the sequence's own termination
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15888                                             ; and why the visible output varied
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15889                                             ; between runs (the exact corruption
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15890                                             ; pattern depends on residual memory
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15891                                             ; state from whatever ran immediately
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15892                                             ; before). Redirected to TSTCBUF2, not
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15893                                             ; TSTCBUF, specifically because TSTCBUF
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15894                                             ; already holds this test's own source
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15895                                             ; string ("1 2 +") - redirecting to the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15896                                             ; same buffer would let WORD overwrite
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15897                                             ; the very source text still being
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15898                                             ; parsed.
