                      (   unit_tests.asm):16243         ; Tools test harness (glossary section 3.18). WORDS depends
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16244         ; directly on LATEST (confirmed via its own code: it walks from
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16245         ; LATEST until the chain terminates at 0) - the same real, pre-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16246         ; COLD dependency section 3.17's own TSTEVALUATE was found to
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16247         ; need, so this section's own WORDS test redirects LATEST too,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16248         ; applying that lesson from the start rather than rediscovering
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16249         ; it. All three words produce visible output, so all apply the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16250         ; SERIALPOLL-conditional split established in section 3.1.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16251         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16252         ; .S prints the ENTIRE real data stack, including whatever this
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16253         ; whole calling chain (TSTRUNNER and everything above it) already
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16254         ; left there before this test even started - unlike every other
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16255         ; test in this session, there's no way to know the full, exact
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16256         ; output in advance. This test's own verification is deliberately
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16257         ; narrower as a result: confirms the core, documented guarantee
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16258         ; directly (the stack is genuinely unchanged afterward, non-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16259         ; destructive for real) plus, in interrupt mode only (where the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16260         ; first characters queued are unambiguously this test's own top
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16261         ; value, since .S starts from the current top of stack), that the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16262         ; very first characters match - rather than attempting to predict
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16263         ; or verify the complete printed output.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16264         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16265         ; DUMP carries real, already-documented bug-fix history: a prior
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16266         ; version's ASCII column read past the actual byte count on a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16267         ; partial final line, showing garbage characters for the unused
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16268         ; portion - fixed via DUVALID tracking. This section's own test
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16269         ; specifically dumps a non-multiple-of-16 byte count (5), the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16270         ; exact scenario that bug affected, verifying the ASCII column's
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16271         ; own blanking for the remaining, invalid columns.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16272         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16273         
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16274         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16275         ; TSTDOTS - unit test for .S. Pushes two known values (no guard
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16276         ; sentinel below them, since .S would print that too), calls .S,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16277         ; and verifies the stack is genuinely unchanged afterward - the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16278         ; core, documented "non-destructive" guarantee, confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16279         ; directly rather than inferred. In interrupt mode specifically,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16280         ; also confirms the very first characters queued match the top
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16281         ; value's own printed form (unambiguous, since .S starts from
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16282         ; the current top of stack); polling mode only confirms some
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16283         ; output occurred, given EMITCH alone can't distinguish this
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16284         ; test's own output from whatever the rest of the real stack
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16285         ; contributes afterward.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):16286         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
