                      (    forth6809.asm):02999         ; NONAME (":NONAME", CORE EXT): like COLON, but deliberately skips
                      (    forth6809.asm):03000         ; HEADER entirely - no WORD call (consumes no name from the input),
                      (    forth6809.asm):03001         ; no new header written at DPHERE, and LATEST is left completely
                      (    forth6809.asm):03002         ; untouched. That's the ANS-required "no-name" definition: never
                      (    forth6809.asm):03003         ; findable by FIND, never linked into the dictionary chain at all.
                      (    forth6809.asm):03004         ; In this subroutine-threaded system the execution token IS the code
                      (    forth6809.asm):03005         ; address (no separate CFA indirection, unlike CREATE's DODOES
                      (    forth6809.asm):03006         ; trampoline), so the xt ANS requires :NONAME to leave on the stack
                      (    forth6809.asm):03007         ; is simply CODEHERE at this instant - identical to what HEREW
                      (    forth6809.asm):03008         ; returns - pushed BEFORE compilation of the body begins, matching
                      (    forth6809.asm):03009         ; where ANS says :NONAME produces it. CSP is snapshotted AFTER that
                      (    forth6809.asm):03010         ; push (mirroring COLON's own CSP snapshot, taken after HEADER's
                      (    forth6809.asm):03011         ; transient pushes/pops have already netted back to baseline) so
                      (    forth6809.asm):03012         ; SEMI's control-flow consistency check at ";" only catches a
                      (    forth6809.asm):03013         ; genuinely unbalanced IF/DO etc. left over from the body, not the
                      (    forth6809.asm):03014         ; xt itself, which is meant to still be there when ";" returns.
                      (    forth6809.asm):03015         ; SEMI itself needs no changes: its unsmudge-the-word-at-LATEST step
                      (    forth6809.asm):03016         ; still targets whatever LATEST already was (the previous NAMED
                      (    forth6809.asm):03017         ; word, untouched by this routine) - a harmless no-op there, since a
                      (    forth6809.asm):03018         ; normal definition is already unsmudged by the time any later
                      (    forth6809.asm):03019         ; definition's SEMI runs.
DFD3 DC08             (    forth6809.asm):03020         NONAME:     LDD   CODEHERE
DFD5 3606             (    forth6809.asm):03021                     PSHU  D
DFD7 DD3D             (    forth6809.asm):03022                     STD   CURXT             ; BUG FIX: RECURSE needs this word's own xt
                      (    forth6809.asm):03023                                             ; (see RECURSE and COLON's matching fix) -
                      (    forth6809.asm):03024                                             ; :NONAME deliberately never touches LATEST
                      (    forth6809.asm):03025                                             ; (correctly, per ANS - a :NONAME word is
                      (    forth6809.asm):03026                                             ; never findable/linked), but RECURSE used to
                      (    forth6809.asm):03027                                             ; unconditionally walk LATEST's header to find
                      (    forth6809.asm):03028                                             ; the xt to recurse into. Inside a :NONAME
                      (    forth6809.asm):03029                                             ; body that meant RECURSE compiled a call to
                      (    forth6809.asm):03030                                             ; whatever NAMED word happened to be defined
                      (    forth6809.asm):03031                                             ; most recently - a completely unrelated word
                      (    forth6809.asm):03032                                             ; - rather than this one. Confirmed against
                      (    forth6809.asm):03033                                             ; Annex F's RECURSE test (":NONAME ... CASE
                      (    forth6809.asm):03034                                             ; ... RECURSE ... ENDCASE ; CONSTANT rn2"):
                      (    forth6809.asm):03035                                             ; every case that actually took the RECURSE
                      (    forth6809.asm):03036                                             ; path failed ttester's "WRONG NUMBER OF
                      (    forth6809.asm):03037                                             ; RESULTS" (recursing into a different word
                      (    forth6809.asm):03038                                             ; with a different stack effect), while
                      (    forth6809.asm):03039                                             ; ordinary named RECURSE tests (rn1, 12's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):03040                                             ; earlier definitions) were unaffected, since
                      (    forth6809.asm):03041                                             ; LATEST is correct for those. STD here costs
                      (    forth6809.asm):03042                                             ; nothing extra (D already holds CODEHERE).
