                      (    forth6809.asm):04699                     ; of their high bytes, BMI on a sign flip). That's wrong in
                      (    forth6809.asm):04700                     ; general: a signed 16-bit difference's sign bit flips at
                      (    forth6809.asm):04701                     ; TWO points on the 65536-value ring, not one - at the true
                      (    forth6809.asm):04702                     ; limit (correct) AND at the antipodal point exactly halfway
                      (    forth6809.asm):04703                     ; around (spurious, nothing to do with limit at all). Any
                      (    forth6809.asm):04704                     ; small/ordinary loop range never reaches that second point,
                      (    forth6809.asm):04705                     ; so GD2 and friends still passed - but Annex F's GD8 (its
                      (    forth6809.asm):04706                     ; "ustep"/"step" constants are deliberately sized to march
                      (    forth6809.asm):04707                     ; the index across nearly the whole MAX-UINT/MAX-INT range)
                      (    forth6809.asm):04708                     ; hits the spurious antipodal flip first every time, exiting
                      (    forth6809.asm):04709                     ; at exactly half the correct iteration count (128 instead
                      (    forth6809.asm):04710                     ; of 256) - confirmed by simulating both the old algorithm
                      (    forth6809.asm):04711                     ; and the fix below against GD8's own 4 cases, and checking
                      (    forth6809.asm):04712                     ; the fix still agrees with the old algorithm (and with
                      (    forth6809.asm):04713                     ; hardware-confirmed behavior) on GD2, a limit=0 decreasing
                      (    forth6809.asm):04714                     ; loop, and an exact-landing case, where the two never
                      (    forth6809.asm):04715                     ; differed. Correct, general test: compare old_u and new_u
                      (    forth6809.asm):04716                     ; as UNSIGNED values and ask which direction they moved -
                      (    forth6809.asm):04717                     ; crossing limit means this unsigned "distance from limit"
