F4E9 DD08             (    forth6809.asm):06527                     STD   CODEHERE          ; where WORD is about to write its parsed
                      (    forth6809.asm):06528                                             ; text. Without this, the compiled path
                      (    forth6809.asm):06529                                             ; below would compile "JSR DOSTR" (3 bytes)
                      (    forth6809.asm):06530                                             ; directly at CODEHERE - the same address
                      (    forth6809.asm):06531                                             ; WORD just used - overwriting the first 2
                      (    forth6809.asm):06532                                             ; characters of the very text being staged,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06533                                             ; before the copy loop even runs. Reserving
                      (    forth6809.asm):06534                                             ; the gap first means the text lands exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):06535                                             ; where it needs to end up, and the trampoline
                      (    forth6809.asm):06536                                             ; safely goes in front of it instead of on
                      (    forth6809.asm):06537                                             ; top of it.
